Subject: [PATCH v2 0/9] sparc32: repair cache hooks, mappings and TLB
 tracking

I am submitting nine fixes for SPARC32 cache geometry, user-page copying,
cache hooks, mappings and CPU-mask tracking. They apply to the recorded
linux-sparc for-next commit, independently of my posted bit-lock fix.

Since summer 2026, I have been working on booting and running Linux
reliably on SMP HyperSPARC, with native GDB builds as my main workload.
These fixes came out of that work but address common SPARC32 paths;
I plan to submit the HyperSPARC-specific fixes separately on top.

Changes in v2:
- Patch 2 flushes the source kernel alias before and after copying,
  including lowmem mappings that bypass the kmap cache hooks. This
  addresses the stale supervisor-alias case raised by Sashiko's review.
- Clarify that the historical hardware results predate this change.
  The other eight patches are unchanged.

I previously completed a native GDB 18.1 build on a dual-CPU HyperSPARC
RT626 SPARCstation 20 with 512 MB RAM and a native SPARC32 SMP kernel
containing the combined series and separate platform prerequisites,
without core dumps, livelock or new kernel messages. That integration
run predates this rebase and v2; it is not isolated per-patch validation.

For v2, SMP and UP builds and repeated COW/reuse tests passed under QEMU
SS-20. The tests check copied contents, parent isolation and rewrites
across virtual page colours. QEMU does not validate HyperSPARC cache
alias behaviour; physical validation of the new case remains pending.
Validation kernels include the separate PIL and IPI fixes, not submitted
here. The standalone test source is kept separately from these patches.

The previously posted SuperSPARC demap series remains separate and needs
a follow-up to retain mm_cpumask, consistent with patch 8 here.
HyperSPARC-specific fixes and optimizations are not included.

Codex assisted with preparation, review and local validation.

Magnus Lindholm (9):
  sparc32: inspect every PROM CPU cache geometry
  sparc32: flush the source user alias in copy_user_highpage()
  sparc32: do not flush a NULL address in flush_dcache_folio
  sparc32: flush the cache when a kmap_local mapping is installed
  sparc32: preset modified and referenced bits in kmap PTEs
  sparc32: colour-align private file mappings
  sparc32: implement flush_anon_page
  sparc32: retain mm_cpumask across TLB shootdowns
  sparc32: enroll and order CPUs before switching address spaces

